%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ea1fbb0ab59d4c84a59e909f29a5c4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: DontCallMe::DontCallMe.Data.DayData
  day: 3
  dateLabel: Thursday, 8 October
  weekday: Thu
  shortLabel: "Day 3 \xB7 Thu 8 Oct"
  place: Mangwon-dong, Seoul
  startTime: 16:25
  intro: Midterms are next week. The water came back at noon, and the monitor you
    ordered should arrive any day now.
  ringDelay: 6
  variants:
  - id: scam
    conversation: {fileID: 11400000, guid: dd8f3009526ae4ecea1b3cc941188dfb, type: 2}
    phone: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4a2be0ca92ed64286bd3594736a8d095, type: 2}
    room: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 34704f64ca23c402bbd5d03136cf3325, type: 2}
    directory: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 532f324eb1836452a9c0cf514f56ff8d, type: 2}
    clues:
    - id: courier_notice
      text: Hangang Express's own notice says the monitor cleared customs and arrives
        on Friday, with nothing to pay.
      where: "Chats \u2192 Hangang Express, or the calendar on the wall"
      when:
      - kind: 4
        target: hangang
      - kind: 0
        target: Calendar
    - id: taxes
      text: AliStar's message says the import taxes were included at checkout.
      where: "Chats \u2192 AliStar"
      when:
      - kind: 4
        target: alistar
    - id: number
      text: Hangang Express's number is 1588-5520. The caller's 1588-5502 is one
        digit off and belongs to "KR Clearance Service".
      where: "Desk drawer \u2192 Delivery slip, or Computer \u2192 Check a phone
        number"
      when:
      - kind: 1
        target: Delivery slip
      - kind: 2
        target: 1588-5502
    - id: account_owner
      text: The account belongs to "KR CUSTOMS CLEARANCE", not to Hangang Express.
      where: "Computer \u2192 Check a bank account"
      when:
      - kind: 2
        target: 620-557-301144
      - kind: 3
        target: 620-557-301144
    papers:
    - outcome: 1
      headline: Fake customs desk used leaked AliStar orders
      subhead: The callers knew the item and the tracking number. The parcels had
        already cleared customs.
      body: 'Callers posing as Hangang Express''s "customs clearance desk" phoned
        AliStar customers in Mapo yesterday. They read out each customer''s order
        and tracking number and asked for "unpaid duty" to be paid into an account
        before 5 p.m.


        The details came from last month''s AliStar data
        leak. The parcels had already cleared customs with their taxes paid, and
        the calls came from 1588-5502, one digit off Hangang Express''s real number,
        1588-5520.


        "If duty is due, our own notice says so, with an account
        in our name," a Hangang Express spokesperson said. "We never ask you to pay
        anyone else."'
      verdictNote: You hung up. The parcel had cleared customs, the taxes were included,
        and the number was one digit off.
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 0
      headline: 56,600 won of "duty" on a parcel that was already paid for
      subhead: Scammers with leaked AliStar orders posed as a courier's customs desk.
      body: 'Callers posing as Hangang Express''s "customs clearance desk" phoned
        AliStar customers in Mapo yesterday. They read out each customer''s order
        and tracking number and asked for "unpaid duty" to be paid into an account
        before 5 p.m.


        A Mangwon student paid 56,600 won into an account
        in the name "KR Customs Clearance", opened a week ago. Her monitor had cleared
        customs on Wednesday, its taxes paid by the seller at checkout. It arrived
        this morning.


        "If duty is due, our own notice says so, with an
        account in our name," a Hangang Express spokesperson said. "We never ask
        you to pay anyone else."'
      verdictNote: The courier's notice and AliStar's message both said the taxes
        were paid, and the account wasn't in Hangang Express's name.
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 3
      headline: Customs desk calling? Read the courier's notice
      subhead: Scammers with leaked orders called AliStar customers yesterday.
      body: 'Callers posing as Hangang Express''s "customs clearance desk" phoned
        AliStar customers in Mapo yesterday. They read out each customer''s order
        and tracking number and asked for "unpaid duty" to be paid into an account
        before 5 p.m.


        The details came from last month''s AliStar data
        leak. The parcels had already cleared customs with their taxes paid, and
        the calls came from 1588-5502, one digit off Hangang Express''s real number,
        1588-5520.


        "If duty is due, our own notice says so, with an account
        in our name," a Hangang Express spokesperson said. "We never ask you to pay
        anyone else."'
      verdictNote: Nothing was sent. The courier's own notice would have told you
        the monitor had already cleared customs.
      print: {fileID: 0}
    ruleTitle: Is anything due? Read the courier's own notice
    rule: Courier or customs asking for money? Read the courier's own notice and
      check who owns the number and the account. If the courier says nothing is due,
      nothing is due.
    ruleSource: Seoul Daily, 9 Oct
  - id: legit
    conversation: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5a17a919d848b411b8f363cb15b0d857, type: 2}
    phone: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f6a73e558567c4210a3307ef4d373a6f, type: 2}
    room: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ab53550557ffd4d9ea32ed20fee2339f, type: 2}
    directory: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 02f9f9698de7441c38173bbfcb7635ef, type: 2}
    clues:
    - id: courier_notice
      text: "Hangang Express's own notice says the monitor is held at customs, with
        \u20A956,600 due and the same account."
      where: "Chats \u2192 Hangang Express, or the calendar on the wall"
      when:
      - kind: 4
        target: hangang
      - kind: 0
        target: Calendar
    - id: taxes
      text: AliStar's message says the import taxes were not included.
      where: "Chats \u2192 AliStar"
      when:
      - kind: 4
        target: alistar
    - id: number
      text: 1588-5520, the number calling you, is Hangang Express's official number.
      where: "Desk drawer \u2192 Delivery slip, or Computer \u2192 Check a phone
        number"
      when:
      - kind: 1
        target: Delivery slip
      - kind: 2
        target: 1588-5520
    - id: account_owner
      text: The account is a virtual account in the name HANGANG EXPRESS (CUSTOMS).
      where: "Computer \u2192 Check a bank account"
      when:
      - kind: 2
        target: 5620-44-018830
      - kind: 3
        target: 5620-44-018830
    papers:
    - outcome: 0
      headline: 'Shopping abroad: when the duty is real'
      subhead: Couriers say more overseas orders are held for duty, and that customers
        are right to check before paying.
      body: 'With cheap overseas shopping booming, Hangang Express says it now holds
        hundreds of parcels a day at Incheon for unpaid duty and VAT, usually because
        the seller didn''t collect the taxes at checkout.


        "When duty is
        due, we send a notice and call from 1588-5520," said Yoon Seora of the courier''s
        customs desk. "The account is always a virtual account in our name." "Customers
        who check that first are doing exactly the right thing."


        Personal
        orders up to US$150 are duty-free. Above that, duty and VAT are due on arrival
        unless the seller collected them.'
      verdictNote: 'The duty was real, and you checked: the courier''s notice, AliStar''s
        message, the official number and the account name all matched.'
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 1
      headline: Real duty notices ignored after a wave of scams
      subhead: Parcels pile up at Incheon as customers hang up on real customs calls.
      body: 'With cheap overseas shopping booming, Hangang Express says it now holds
        hundreds of parcels a day at Incheon for unpaid duty and VAT, usually because
        the seller didn''t collect the taxes at checkout. After weeks of fake customs
        texts, many customers now hang up on the real thing, and dozens of parcels
        were sent back yesterday.


        "When duty is due, we send a notice and
        call from 1588-5520," said Yoon Seora of the courier''s customs desk. "The
        account is always a virtual account in our name." "Check it, by all means.
        But check the facts, not just your nerves."


        Personal orders up
        to US$150 are duty-free. Above that, duty and VAT are due on arrival unless
        the seller collected them.'
      verdictNote: 'This one was real: the courier''s own notice showed the same
        duty and account, and the call came from Hangang Express''s official number.'
      print: {fileID: 0}
    - outcome: 3
      headline: Parcels go back as duty goes unpaid
      subhead: Customers who never decided lost their orders to the return queue.
      body: 'With cheap overseas shopping booming, Hangang Express says it now holds
        hundreds of parcels a day at Incheon for unpaid duty and VAT, usually because
        the seller didn''t collect the taxes at checkout.


        "When duty is
        due, we send a notice and call from 1588-5520," said Yoon Seora of the courier''s
        customs desk. "The account is always a virtual account in our name."


        Personal
        orders up to US$150 are duty-free. Above that, duty and VAT are due on arrival
        unless the seller collected them.'
      verdictNote: The duty was real, and the evidence was in the courier's notice
        and AliStar's message. Deciding in time matters too.
      print: {fileID: 0}
    ruleTitle: Pay duty only to the courier
    rule: Real duty shows up in the courier's own notice, with an account in the
      courier's name. When they match the call, paying is safe.
    ruleSource: Seoul Daily, 9 Oct
